@O/<Jumping Volley>@
An acrobatic shot: a volley struck
while jumping.

@0/<Drive Shot>@
A shot hit with topspin on the ball.
Its trademark is a sharp dip.

@O/<Volley>@
Striking a ball in the air directly,
without controlling it first.

@O/<Lob Shot>@
A soft shot chipped over the keeper's
head.

@O/<Ball Retention>@
Keeping hold of the ball so that the
opposition cannot get it.

@O/<Killer Pass>@
A decisive pass that often leads to a
goal.

@O/<One-Touch>@
Kicking a moving ball without first
controlling it.

@O/<Clearance>@
A defender kicking the ball out of a
danger zone to get out of trouble.

@O/<Delaying>@
Slowing the opposition's attack to buy
time for your side to get organised.

@O/<Catching>@
The most important goalkeeping skill:
safely catching shots and crosses.

@O/<Shot-Stopping>@
A goalkeeper diving to keep out shots
and other chances for the opposition.

@O/<Punching>@
A goalkeeper skill: punching away balls
that cannot be caught.

@O/<Fumble>@
Failing to catch the ball cleanly and
letting it spill loose.

@O/<Pitch>@
Explains terms used for areas of the
football pitch.

@O/<Goal Area>@
The area in front of goal, 5.5 metres
deep and 18.3 metres wide.

@O/<Goal Line>@
The two shorter lines marking out the
rectangular pitch.

@O/<Penalty Spot>@
The mark 11 metres out from the goal.
Penalty kicks are taken from here.

@O/<Normal>@
Ordinary midfield defence in a match,
without using the Zonal Press.

@O/<Competitions>@
Explains technical terms for football
competition and match formats.

@O/<Away Match>@
A match played in the rival club's
home town.

@O/<Seed>@
Priority treatment in knockouts, often
meaning a bye from the first round.

@O/<Home and Away>@
Settling a tie with two matches, one at
your home town and one in theirs.

@O/<League>@
A round-robin among the clubs entered
in the competition.

@O/<Striker>@
A player who is good at scoring goals.
Also called a goal-getter.

@O/<Attacking MF>@
A midfielder who focuses on attack.
Also called an offensive half.

@O/<Rules>@
Explains technical terms about the
rules of football.

@O/<Yellow Card>@
The card shown by a referee to caution
a player.

@O/<In Play>@
Play that takes place while the ball is
on the pitch and play is continuing.

@O/<Onside>@
A position from which a player may play
legitimately, beyond the offside zone.

@O/<Red Card>@
The card a referee shows when sending a
player off.

@O/<Other>@
Explains other technical terms relating
to football.

@O/<Eye Contact>@
Players checking their next move with
each other through eye contact.

@O/<Captain's Armband>@
The band the team captain wears on
their arm.

@O/<Supporters>@
The people who cheer for and back the
club.

@O/<Dead Space>@
Space the opposition has under control
that cannot be used for attacking.

@O/<Behind the Strikers>@
The player just a little deeper than
the strikers, called the "1.5 line".

@O/<Hat-Trick>@
When one player scores 3 goals in a
single match.

@O/<Fantasista>@
A player with rich creativity in their
play.

@O/<Finish>@
Mostly means the shot, the last action
of a move.

@O/<Hooligans>@
Extreme supporters who run riot during
matches.

@O/<Heads-Up Play>@
Raising your head when you have the
ball to get a good look around.

